cal for anyone that wants  to learn how to make the most out of  their microbiome data  so the unique part of this is that you  actually get to see  the code and try to run it yourself  so you learn about the code you see the  different outputs  and then you can actually try it by  yourself  so here we have created a way for us to  take the scripts and run them in our  studio on the cloud and really  eliminates a lot of the  challenges that people have with  setting up their environment so here for  example you can see i've analyzed the  data set  and i can see the composition of my  sample  based on proportion or based on  abundance  so this is a little bit of an overview  of some of these tools on how to  register again many of these resources  are completely free  so if you don't want to join the program  and you don't have maybe  the time or you want to do this on your  own pace  you can register here for free start  learning and when the time comes you  will see  different types of additional in-depth  resources like actual research  capabilities of the platform where you  can upload your own data and manage it  using  ftp and on the coding  we also have some advanced course work  like machine learning and data science  that could get you farther along with  the data that you have  thank you alia so there is a question  from iodine day  is it possible for one to jump directly  on the core metagenomics where we can  use the actual  r scripts yeah so as i showed  the same r scripts are offered there in  any kind of processing of data  it's not the scripts that typically  limit you  it's the infrastructure so if the data  is big  and many of the current studies include  hundreds if not thousands of samples  and the analysis you can do them on your  computer but unless you have a server  stack  you're going to be waiting for a long  time for those pipelines to finish so  that's why we have a lot of these  pipelines implemented on our big data  high performance computing  infrastructure for you to be able to  work with real data sets  but once the data sets are percent  processed and they're ready as a table  you can then do the downstream analysis  and visualization  in r and in python and that is a big  part of what we will do in the program  as well  first of all understanding the logic why  are we doing what we are doing  and what do these visualizations mean  and then doing it  ourselves in r and learning how to  manipulate the data  wrangle it visualize and interpret  uh thank you so much elia so i would  want you all to  go ahead and join our social media  groups  so we are having an active group in  linkedin  and if you go through the group you can  see that this is a group not only for  students or researchers but  you would see that there are a lot of uh  scientists who are joining us in this  group from all  around the world so this gives an  opportunity to be part of a larger  community  as well as we have a group in facebook  so whichever platform  is easy for you please go ahead and join  our platforms  and now to clear some of the doubts that  a lot of you are having regarding the  registration  so if you are already registered on edut  bio info i'm putting the link in the  chat  then this is the link to check out so  you can note  that here is a 150 dollar the price  there is a 33 percent discount that  would be emailed to you  if you have already shared your email id  or if you were already registered for  this  program so you would have to check out  via this link and you can also see the  different courses  that are included as part of this  training program  so please visit this link and if you are  someone who is looking for a scholarship  i  require a scholarship here is a  scholarship  form again i am posting it here in the  chat box  so please make sure to fill up each of  these  fields in the scholarship form and maybe  let us take a look at this together  so that we know what are the different  things